# The counter at the shell's priority (roadmap l4.md L2): it never waits, so
# only the time slices let the shell in; the shell still answers.
program: shell
define: TEST_COUNTER_SAME
define: TEST_THREAD_REPORT
keys: echo one\necho two\n
---
rx286, test build
rx286 shell: type help for the commands
A:\>echo one
one
A:\>echo two
two
A:\>
rx286: thread root ran
rx286: thread printer ran
rx286: thread mouse ran
rx286: thread console ran
rx286: thread kbd ran
rx286: thread fd ran
rx286: thread hd ran
rx286: thread serial ran
rx286: thread sound ran
rx286: thread rtc ran
rx286: thread program ran
rx286: thread counter ran
rx286: thread os ran
rx286: thread os ran
rx286: thread os ran
